        "comments": "The assembly daSonOler1.hap1.1 is based on 117x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Some very weak HiC signal was detected between some of the two pairs of chromosomes, suggesting the species used to be a tetraploid. However, it looks to work as a functional diploid. The order and orientation of the scaffolds on Chromosome_6 0.77 Mbp - 2.34 Mbp, Chromosome_12 25.42 Mbp - 27.57 Mbp, Chromosome_13 21.24 Mbp - 21.86 Mbp, and Chromosome_15 17.25 Mbp - 19.52 Mbp are uncertain.",
